WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.870
West of Gourcy, Burkina Faso,
1984: a barren, laterite surface.

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.230
By 2010, the same land
was productive cropland,

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.170
with a diverse tree parkland.

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:19.110
Farmer Ali Ouédraogo had begun building
stone lines along the contours in 1983.

5
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.290
One cause: drought.

6
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:27.470
Sahel rainfall fell from the wet
1950s to the dry 1970s and 1980s.

7
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.390
The driest year was 1984.

8
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.470
Now the climate is changing.

9
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.170
Will these gains hold in a hotter future?

10
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.530
In this mission, you'll untangle the causes
of degradation on the northern Central

11
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.810
Plateau, and judge the farmers' responses.

12
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.710
Then you'll test alternative futures
for the people who farm there.

13
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.790
Your mission: decide whether the restored
land west of Gourcy will hold in a hotter

14
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.610
future.
